  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46333\", \"PowerToys#48566\", \"PowerToys#34950\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#46333 (Privacy Overlay), which proposes excluding selected windows from screen sharing, recording and screenshots. PowerToys#48566 was closed as a duplicate of it. PowerToys#34950 (Window Masking) asks for the same thing, but its own duplicate pointer went to an unrelated issue. This is not available in PowerToys yet. Subscribe to #46333 and add a 👍 or your use case there. One contributor has built a proof of concept based on the Windows API SetWindowDisplayAffinity with WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE. They found that calling it directly from another process is blocked, so the PoC uses an injected hook DLL. In the meantime, the open-source tools Invisiwind and winhider, which are mentioned in #34950, do a similar thing. They don't detect newly opened windows. You can also share a single window instead of the whole screen.\"}",
